  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "10. Shooting Phase",
    "ruleNumber": "10.07",
    "summary": "An Unengaged unit can select this mode if it has an [INDIRECT FIRE] weapon and has made no Advance move this turn. Resolve the attacks using Making Attacks. The unit's [INDIRECT FIRE] weapons can pick targets their firers cannot see, and those targets receive the Benefit of Cover. Hit rolls cannot be rerolled, and unmodified 1–5 miss. Use 1–3 instead if a friendly unit sees the target and the firing unit Remained Stationary this turn. The unit loses eligibility for the rest of the phase after shooting.",
